      { "label": "License", "values": ["Apache-2.0", "Apache-2.0", "Proprietary", "BSD-3 (community)"] }
    ],
    "jab": "Para was designed to provide a straightforward developer experience and is optimized for LLM-based workflows and rapid prototyping. Para is a good fit if you ask yourself any of the following questions:",
    "questions": [
      "What if I don't want to manage a full PostgreSQL cluster?", 
      "What if my schema is not clarified yet or my data is too dynamic?",
      "What if I want to connect a no-code solution to my backend?",
      "What if I need to prototype an app quickly with a set-it-and-forget-it backend?"
    ]
  },
  "sdks": {
    "headline": "Use the client you know",
    "subtext": "All Para clients share the same REST API. Create, read, update, and delete a user, then search users with one query.",
    "tabsLabel": "Para client SDK examples",
    "exampleLabel": "SDK code example",
    "sourceLabel": "View SDK source",
    "securityNote": "Keep secret keys on trusted servers. Browser and mobile apps should leave the secret key blank, sign in, and use the permissions granted to that user.",
    "tabs": [
      {
        "id": "java",
        "label": "Java",
